      "may_quay": "zoom-ra",
      "chuyen_canh": {"kieu": "toi-den", "thoi_luong": 0.5},
      "lop": [
        {"anh": "nhan-vat/max__suy-nghi__dung.png", "vi_tri": [0.22, 0.86], "neo": "day", "co": 0.2,
         "hieu_ung": "mo-dan", "tre": 0.0, "lien_tuc": "lac"},
        {"anh": "dao-cu/bo-nao.png", "vi_tri": [0.62, 0.48], "co": 0.16,
         "hieu_ung": "phong-to", "tre": 1.6, "lien_tuc": "tho", "am_thanh": "am-thanh/pop.wav"}
      ],
      "chu": [
        {"noi_dung": "PROSPECT THEORY", "vi_tri": [0.62, 0.18], "co": 96, "mau": "#1E3A8A",
         "vien": 8, "mau_vien": "#FFFFFF", "hieu_ung": "bat-len", "tre": 5.4, "am_thanh": "am-thanh/ding.wav"}
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "c05",
      "phan": "giai-thich",
      "loi": "Its key idea: a loss hurts more than a gain of the same size feels good. This is called loss aversion.",
      "nen": "#FFFFFF",
      "may_quay": {"kieu": "rung", "muc": 0.004},
      "chuyen_canh": {"kieu": "zoom-vao", "thoi_luong": 0.4},
      "lop": [
        {"anh": "dao-cu/can-lech.png", "vi_tri": [0.45, 0.5], "co": 0.28,
         "hieu_ung": "roi-xuong", "tre": 0.3, "am_thanh": "am-thanh/pop.wav"},
        {"anh": "nhan-vat/max__so-hai__dung.png", "vi_tri": [0.84, 0.86], "neo": "day", "co": 0.15,
         "hieu_ung": "truot-trai", "tre": 1.2, "lien_tuc": "run"}
      ],
      "chu": [
        {"noi_dung": "LOSS AVERSION", "vi_tri": [0.45, 0.13], "co": 110, "mau": "#E53935",
         "hieu_ung": "go-chu", "tre": 4.8, "am_thanh": "am-thanh/tick.wav"}
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "c06",
      "phan": "giai-thich",
      "loi": "So selling a winner feels like locking in a win. Selling a loser means admitting the loss is real. Hold it, and it is only a loss on paper.",
